# Byte stability is a requirement here, not a preference.
# The four frozen specifications are verified by SHA-256 (CLAUDE.md §0, and the
# hashes recorded during the Stage 0 amendment pass). Letting Git rewrite line
# endings on checkout would change those bytes and invalidate every recorded
# hash, so line endings are pinned to LF in both the index and the working tree
# on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the specifications, so a future change to the global rule cannot
# silently affect them.
*.md text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
